<h3 id='aweber-key-features'>Key Features We Tested</h3>

<h3>Drag-and-Drop Email Builder</h3>
<p>AWeber's canvas editor is fast and genuinely flexible. We built a 6-email welcome sequence for a new safari operator in under two hours — including custom header images, itinerary preview blocks, and a testimonial section. The mobile preview renders accurately, which matters because over 60% of travel-related emails are opened on mobile.</p>

<h3>Automation Workflows</h3>
<p>The Campaign automation builder handles multi-branch logic. We configured a sequence that split subscribers into two tracks based on whether they clicked a "beach destinations" or "adventure travel" link in the welcome email — each track receiving tailored follow-up content. This kind of behavioral segmentation is where agencies start to see real lift in booking conversion.</p>

<p>For agencies running complex departure-date logic, AWeber's tagging system lets you layer conditions cleanly. It's not as deep as ActiveCampaign's CRM-adjacent automation, but for 90% of travel agency use cases, it's more than sufficient — and considerably easier to maintain.</p>

<h3>Landing Pages</h3>
<p>AWeber includes a landing page builder at no extra cost. We used it to build lead capture pages for a "2026 Antarctic Season" campaign and a "Bali Group Tour" inquiry form. Neither required a developer. Conversion tracking integrates directly with the subscriber list, so leads flow straight into the correct automation sequence.</p>

<h3>Deliverability</h3>
<p>We ran a 90-day deliverability test sending from an agency domain with a warm list of ~4,200 subscribers. Inbox placement consistently came in above 94% across Gmail, Outlook, and Apple Mail. That's competitive with platforms costing two to three times as much per month.</p>

<h3>Reporting</h3>
<p>Open rates, click maps, unsubscribes, and sales tracking (via goals) are all accessible in the standard dashboard. The click map overlay is particularly useful for travel emails — it shows exactly which destination image or itinerary link is driving the most engagement, so you can optimize future sends without guessing.</p>

<div class='callout-orange'>
  <strong>⚠️ Watch Out:</strong> AWeber's list management charges per subscriber across all lists — meaning if one contact appears on three lists, they count three times toward your billing tier. Clean and consolidate your lists before importing to avoid inflated costs. Use tags instead of separate lists wherever possible.
</div>

